Description: Secrets manager stack — pass, pam-gnupg, pass-secret-service
 Wires up a distro-wide secrets stack: pass(1) as the password store,
 pass-secret-service exposing it over the org.freedesktop.secrets D-Bus API
 (libsecret apps, e.g. Firefox saved logins), and pam-gnupg unlocking the
 GnuPG key with the login password.
 .
 Patches /etc/pam.d/greetd and /etc/pam.d/gtklock to preset the gpg-agent
 passphrase cache on login and screen-unlock. Ships default
 ~/.gnupg/gpg-agent.conf, a paperweight-passmenu wofi picker bound to
 $mod+p, and paperweight-secrets-init(1) to guide first-time setup
 (GPG key generation is left to the user — never done silently).
 .
 paperweight-secrets-sync bridges the CLI and D-Bus worlds: it mirrors
 regular pass(1) entries into pass-secret-service's store as symlinks so
 apps can see them too; paperweight-passmenu already shows app-created
 secrets by their D-Bus Label. Run after adding CLI passwords you want
 visible to apps.
